Dario Amodei writes that AI will be better than humans at essentially everything. Brian Green says that is simply not correct.

Benjamin Crockett is joined by Brian Green of the Markkula Center for Applied Ethics at Santa Clara University, Brett Robinson of the McGrath Institute for Church Life at Notre Dame, and Devin Patel of the Joseph Rainey Center for Public Policy. They read "The Adolescence of Technology" together and keep returning to the work no machine performs. Caring for a child. Sitting with an elderly parent. Work that brings dignity to the person doing it and the person receiving it.

For all those curious about the world of tomorrow and how to navigate the crucial choices presented by emerging technology, guided by the practical and timeless wisdom of the Catholic faith, join the Catholic Futurist Podcast.

